(281, 'e35a3336-5a53-4042-b5a8-b2f5aec36809', 'Hotel South View', 'hotel-south-view', 10, 'The Hyatt Regency Delhi is a hotel in New Delhi, India, opened in 1983. It is the largest 5-star hotel in North India, in terms of number of rooms, with 495 rooms. It is located in Bhikaji Cama Place, near Chanakyapuri, in South Delhi. It is managed by Hyatt.', 'The Hyatt Regency Delhi is a hotel in New Delhi, India, opened in 1983. It is the largest 5-star hotel in North India, in terms of number of rooms, with 495 rooms. It is located in Bhikaji Cama Place, near Chanakyapuri, in South Delhi. It is managed by Hyatt.\n\n\n== History ==\n\nAsian Hotels (North) Ltd was incorporated in 1980 and was promoted by R S Saraf, R K Jatia, Chaman Lal Gupta, three Non-Resident Indians together with Sushil Gupta and Shiv Jatia, their Indian Associates. The builders enter', NULL, 'Delhi', NULL, 'India', 28.5471742, 77.2494125, 5372987682, 'node', NULL, NULL, 'published', 0.00, 0, 0, 'osm', NULL, '2026-07-29 12:09:28', '2026-07-31 15:15:23'),
