(1228, '03b60528-ab36-4736-b222-ad3552bdd5aa', 'Ashok Stambh', 'ashok-stambh', 5, 'The Bhaisali metro station is an underground Meerut Metro station on the Delhi–Meerut RRTS corridor serving Bhaisali in the central area of Meerut in Uttar Pradesh, India. It serves as a halt for Meerut Metro trains that run at a speed of 120 kilometres (75 mi)/h. The RRTS trains, which do not stop here, pass through the station at a speed of 160 kilometres (99 mi)/h. The station is constructed, owned and operated by the National Capital Region Transport Corporation (NCRTC). The station was inaugurated on 22 February 2026.', 'The Bhaisali metro station is an underground Meerut Metro station on the Delhi–Meerut RRTS corridor (also known as the Namo Bharat corridor) serving Bhaisali in the central area of Meerut in Uttar Pradesh, India. It serves as a halt for Meerut Metro trains that run at a speed of 120 kilometres (75 mi)/h. The RRTS trains, which do not stop here, pass through the station at a speed of 160 kilometres (99 mi)/h. The station is constructed, owned and operated by the National Capital Region Transport ', NULL, 'Delhi', NULL, 'India', 28.6171085, 77.2100700, 1184982373, 'way', NULL, NULL, 'published', 5.00, 1, 0, 'osm', NULL, '2026-07-29 12:09:41', '2026-08-01 10:54:56'),
