(1294, '2bb3e508-99e8-4732-8378-58310fd9cefd', 'Varasiddhi Vinayakar Temple', 'varasiddhi-vinayakar-temple', 1, 'The Varasiddhi Vinayakar Temple in Besant Nagar, Chennai, India is a Hindu temple, located near the beach in Besant Nagar. It is dedicated to the Hindu god Vinayaka or Ganesha. The temple participates in activities such as feeding the poor and holds poojas frequently.', 'The Varasiddhi Vinayakar Temple in Besant Nagar, Chennai, India is a Hindu temple, located near the beach in Besant Nagar. It is dedicated to the Hindu god Vinayaka or Ganesha. The temple participates in activities such as feeding the poor and holds poojas frequently.\nThe first Kumbabhishekam (consecration) of the temple after extension activity was held in April, 1979 before which the idol was being worshiped at a site opposite the present site of the temple, within the CPWD Quarters compound. ', NULL, 'Chennai', NULL, 'India', 12.9791978, 80.1811044, 280499221, 'node', NULL, NULL, 'published', 0.00, 0, 0, 'osm', NULL, '2026-07-29 12:17:45', '2026-07-29 13:12:25'),
