(1457, '3d3d6fcb-27e2-411b-af45-15f82634c10a', 'Sunrise Boys Hostel', 'sunrise-boys-hostel', 5, 'Telugu Christians or Telugu Kraistava are ethnic-Telugus who follow Christianity. They form the third largest religious minority in the Indian states of Andhra Pradesh and Telangana. According to the 2001 Census of India, there are over a million Christians in Andhra Pradesh, constituting around 1.51% of the state\'s population.', 'Telugu Christians or Telugu Kraistava (Telugu: తెలుగు క్రైస్తవులు, romanized: Telugu Kraistavulu) are ethnic-Telugus who follow Christianity. They form the third largest religious minority in the Indian states of Andhra Pradesh and Telangana. According to the 2001 Census of India, there are over a million Christians in Andhra Pradesh, constituting around 1.51% of the state\'s population.\nMost Telugu Christians are Protestant, belonging to major Indian Protestant denominations such as the predomin', NULL, 'ongole', NULL, 'India', 15.5121804, 80.0416210, 12596501211, 'node', NULL, NULL, 'published', 0.00, 0, 0, 'osm', NULL, '2026-07-31 19:05:19', '2026-08-01 16:44:04'),
